reranker_config_notes:
Two-stage pipeline encouraged: dense retrieval (Faiss HNSW, 200-500 candidates) -> light-weight cross-encoder reranker on top-32. Reranker experiments run:
- model A: cross-encoder-large (GPU) high precision, p50 latency 120ms for 32 candidates, cost high;
- model B: distilled cross-encoder (CPU optimized) p50 300ms, much cheaper;
- model C: distilled + early-exit (adaptive) with p95 650ms. Team leaning to candidate size 64 -> rerank top 16 to reduce cost. Also exploring reranker quantization and batching for amortized GPU cost. Need Redwood suggestion on model fallback rules if Dedicated GPUs saturated.
